; Playwright workspace + browser-loadable OCaml backends for the shared browser driver, HTML
; target, and Playwright tests. This suite needs a Node runtime and the locked
; npm workspace (`npm ci` in this directory, see test/README.md), so its runtime targets are opt-in
; rather than part of `@runtest` -- mirroring test/node_pty's own opt-in convention.

(executable
 (name jsoo_bridge)
 (modules jsoo_bridge)
 (modes js)
 (libraries tessera_test_web_bridge_runner js_of_ocaml))

; A confirmed, resolved choice: `strings` on the installed dune 3.24.2 binary confirms `module_systems` accepts
; `(esm .mjs)`, emitting real ES modules (`import`/`export`) loadable via `<script type="module">`/
; dynamic `import()` with no bundler or shim -- distinct from test/node_pty/dune's existing
; `(module_systems commonjs)`, which stays untouched (that suite is Node-only and correct as-is).

(melange.emit
 (target melange-output)
 (alias web-render-melange)
 (modules melange_bridge)
 (module_systems
  (esm mjs))
 (libraries tessera_test_web_bridge_runner))

; The per-case ordered-frame JSONL golden generator (native only). An explicit developer command
